/-!
# The exact Schreier word problem for source M₁

The candidate table uses the right ATLAS action, rooted at point 1206 (index
1205). The breadth-first tree uses letters x, y, y⁻¹ in that order. Symbols
1, 2, 3 are the three literal source subgroup words. Symbols 4 through 2062
are the non-tree positive edges, ordered first by their starting point and
then by x, y. Tree edges contribute the empty word.

`initialRelator` lists the seven relator loops at each of the 2058 points,
then three equations identifying the protected symbols with their Schreier
words. These are definitions only: this module does not assert that the
initial or reduced relators hold. The separate Schreier proof must establish
the telescoping equalities in the abstract presentation. In particular no
permutation table or computational index is assumed to be a coset cover.

Source: John Bray's ATLAS `HeG1-P1.M`, the three literal M₁ generators and
seven uncommented relators; original files retained in `Held/Model/Source/`.
The generator script in `source/` reproduces the data from those files.
-/

@[expose] public section
